# [SCHC](../wg/schc.html)

## Summary

The SCHC Working Group held its 13th interim meeting of 2026. The session was chaired by Alexander Pelov. The group discussed the status and management of active and expiring working group documents, made plans for the upcoming IETF 127 meeting, and reviewed two technical presentations on updates to the SCHC YANG data model and an ICMPv6 security extension designed to handle LPWAN-specific timer challenges.

---

## WG Document Status & IETF 127 Planning

* **`draft-ietf-schc-8824-update`**: Marco Tiloca confirmed that version 10 addresses all pending comments from the Vienna session. The draft is ready for submission to the IESG. Alexander Pelov agreed to write the shepherding report and submit the document.
* **`draft-ietf-schc-access-control`**: Ana Minaburo and Laurent Toutain confirmed that this work remains active but needs updates to realign with the YANG data model. Ana Minaburo committed to publishing a new version to prevent its expiration.
* **Draft Cleanup**: Alexander Pelov noted several drafts are expired or close to expiration (including the ICMPv6 compression draft and universal options draft). He urged authors to upload minor updates to keep them active before a planned end-of-year cleanup.
* **IETF 127 Prep**: Alexander Pelov proposed keeping the 1.5-hour meeting format for IETF 127, requesting a slot scheduled no later than Thursday. Éric Vyncke agreed that the 1.5-hour duration is appropriate.

